现在我们转向Representation来决定系统可以顺利地改变什么。

605
00:39:28,197 --> 00:39:32,254
A representation is the form in which the system handles media.
表示是系统处理媒体的形式。

606
00:39:32,254 --> 00:39:35,832
Pixels are direct, but high-resolution video contains enormous redundancy.
像素是直接的，但高分辨率视频包含巨大的冗余。

607
00:39:35,832 --> 00:39:39,151
Latent representations compress visual information into a smaller space.
潜在表征将视觉信息压缩到更小的空间中。

608
00:39:39,151 --> 00:39:43,209
Discrete visual tokens turn image or video content into sequences that
离散视觉标记将图像或视频内容转换为序列

609
00:39:43,209 --> 00:39:48,004
can be modeled alongside language. The creative consequence is that representation creates neighborhoods.
可以与语言一起建模。创造性的结果是代表性创造了社区。

610
00:39:48,004 --> 00:39:53,426
In a useful latent space, nearby points often correspond to related appearances or concepts.
在有用的潜在空间中，附近的点通常对应于相关的外观或概念。

611
00:39:53,426 --> 00:39:56,893
That makes interpolation, editing, and controlled variation possible.
这使得插值、编辑和受控变化成为可能。

612
00:39:56,893 --> 00:39:58,737
But compression also discards information.
但压缩也会丢弃信息。

613
00:39:58,737 --> 00:40:04,307
